# Prologue — "Cold Open" (master_plan.md §2.6, story_bible.md §prologue).
# Dr. Sova teaches Ground diegetically; ends with one scripted misheard
# line, immediately disclosed. Pass 15 v0 scope: proves the DSL/compiler/
# runtime pipeline end-to-end, not the full authored prologue.

START node_briefing

== node_briefing ==
npc.sova: Before we start, a simple exercise. Hold still, hold quiet, and tell me what's true.
+claim.sova_taught_ground

-> node_choice

== node_choice ==
npc.sova: Tell me — what did you hear just now, down the hall?
choice "The heating pipes, ticking." [procedural] -> node_pipes
choice "Footsteps. Someone was there." [pressing] -> node_footsteps

== node_pipes ==
player: The heating pipes, ticking.
+claim.player_heard(player, heard_sound, heating_pipes)
npc.sova: Correct. Ground told you the truth before I even had to.

-> node_close

== node_footsteps ==
player: Footsteps. Someone was there.
+claim.player_heard(player, heard_sound, footsteps)
drift: "Footsteps. Someone was there." [doubt]
npc.sova: There was no one in that hall. That's the lesson — not everything you hear is real.

-> node_close

== node_close ==
npc.sova: Ground when you doubt. It costs you time, never dignity.
+claim.sova_closing_lesson(npc.sova, lesson_theme, ground_costs_time_not_dignity)

-> END
